# Figma Design Fidelity Protocol

When modifying or implementing layout structures, you must treat user-provided design specifications as strict, uncompromisable constraints.

* **Layout Geometry:** Use strict CSS grid or flexbox positioning scales. Ensure component dimensions, margins, and padding line up precisely with design specifications.
* **Token Consistency:** Utilize designated global styling tokens exclusively for colours, font weighting, sizing metrics, and responsive breakpoints. Never introduce hardcoded inline styles.
* **Pixel-Perfect Alignment:** Evaluate how visual boundaries, element alignments, and typography line up relative to parent containers to maintain an exact match with the Figma layout blueprint.
